{"id": "lyft-wheelchair-complaint-corrections", "title": "Lyft’s missing wheelchair-ride complaints and the fee offsets California upheld", "seconds": 62.3, "voice": "elevenlabs:iPYqcpY8j8Ap4jUf28I3", "narrator": "Michael", "tempo": 1.044, "made": "2026-11-27", "key": "37f8bcc49ac35c21", "words": 152, "beats": [{"scene": "p", "kind": "hook", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "Lyft reported zero wheelchair-accessible ride complaints in San Francisco across two quarters in 2023.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 7.06, "shot": "s0", "visual": {"type": "hook", "words": ["Zero", "complaints"], "sub": "San Francisco’s original report showed zero complaints in two quarters"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.82, 1.21, 2.35, 2.62, 3.1, 3.23, 3.41, 4.4, 4.85, 5.12, 5.64, 5.79, 6.12]}, {"scene": "b", "kind": "record", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "The corrected files show four in the second quarter. All were classified as other.", "t0": 7.28, "t1": 12.28, "shot": "s1", "visual": {"type": "record", "source": "correct", "layout": "table", "heading": "San Francisco complaints", "context": "Original → corrected", "rows": [{"label": "Q2 2023", "value": "0 → 4"}, {"label": "Q3 2023", "value": "0 → 0"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.54, 0.97, 1.31, 1.78, 1.9, 2.01, 2.33, 3.35, 3.69, 3.86, 4.48, 4.65]}, {"scene": "b", "kind": "record", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "Across San Francisco and Los Angeles, the reported count rose from 10 to 24.", "t0": 12.4, "t1": 17.99, "shot": "s2", "visual": {"type": "record", "source": "correct", "layout": "table", "heading": "Two reporting periods", "context": "San Francisco and Los Angeles", "rows": [{"label": "Original", "value": "10"}, {"label": "Corrected", "value": "24"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.44, 0.69, 1.3, 1.41, 1.68, 2.57, 2.72, 3.18, 3.49, 3.94, 4.17, 4.7, 4.88]}, {"scene": "b", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "Lyft said a new reporting method missed complaints classified as non-safety at intake.", "t0": 18.11, "t1": 23.52, "shot": "s3", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "method", "kicker": "The new reporting method skipped complaints classified as non-safety at intake", "text": "Complaint intake", "mark": "Complaint"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.4, 0.83, 1.0, 1.24, 1.74, 2.1, 2.42, 3.03, 3.71, 3.88, 4.73, 4.85]}, {"scene": "b", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "In 2024, it disclosed the error and said it had returned to manual collection.", "t0": 23.64, "t1": 29.06, "shot": "s4", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "method", "kicker": "The new reporting method skipped complaints classified as non-safety at intake", "text": "Method change", "mark": "Method"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.46, 1.65, 1.81, 2.35, 2.49, 2.86, 3.11, 3.58, 3.75, 3.91, 4.34, 4.46, 4.85]}, {"scene": "b", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]"], "text": "California had already approved more than half a million dollars in San Francisco fee offsets.", "t0": 29.18, "t1": 34.99, "shot": "s5", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "q2", "kicker": "San Francisco’s approved offsets totaled $516,519.15", "text": "Fee offsets", "mark": "Fee"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.74, 0.89, 1.25, 1.76, 1.95, 2.2, 2.53, 2.62, 3.01, 3.78, 3.99, 4.24, 4.92, 5.18]}, {"scene": "b", "kind": "record", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]"], "text": "Over $270,000 came from the third quarter.", "t0": 35.11, "t1": 38.78, "shot": "s6", "visual": {"type": "record", "source": "q3", "layout": "table", "heading": "San Francisco fee offsets", "context": "The state kept both approvals", "rows": [{"label": "Q2 2023", "value": "$245,835.60"}, {"label": "Q3 2023", "value": "$270,683.55"}, {"label": "Combined", "value": "$516,519.15"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.43, 0.85, 1.39, 1.84, 2.35, 2.67, 2.84, 2.95, 3.25]}, {"scene": "o", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[4]"], "text": "Did the state reverse those offsets? In August 2024, it expressly upheld them.", "t0": 39.0, "t1": 45.04, "shot": "s7", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "disposition", "kicker": "The Commission preserved the offsets and distinguished on-demand from pre-scheduled performance", "text": "State decision", "mark": "State"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.3, 0.72, 1.2, 1.47, 2.65, 2.85, 3.16, 3.41, 4.54, 4.71, 5.45, 5.81]}, {"scene": "o", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[4]"], "text": "San Francisco’s on-demand service beat its trip completion threshold.", "t0": 45.16, "t1": 49.1, "shot": "s8", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "disposition", "kicker": "The Commission preserved the offsets and distinguished on-demand from pre-scheduled performance", "text": "On-demand service", "mark": "On-demand"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.96, 1.57, 2.08, 2.34, 2.54, 2.81, 3.34]}, {"scene": "o", "kind": "record", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[4]"], "text": "Pre-scheduled rides completed only 50 percent against a 90 percent minimum.", "t0": 49.22, "t1": 53.97, "shot": "s9", "visual": {"type": "record", "source": "standard", "layout": "table", "heading": "Pre-scheduled service", "context": "San Francisco, Q3 2023", "rows": [{"label": "Completed", "value": "50%"}, {"label": "Threshold", "value": "90%"}, {"label": "Approved offset", "value": "$0"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.87, 1.24, 1.68, 1.94, 2.36, 2.86, 3.23, 3.37, 3.79, 4.24]}, {"scene": "o", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[4]"], "text": "The state approved no pre-scheduled offset in either county for that quarter.", "t0": 54.09, "t1": 58.75, "shot": "s10", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Pre-scheduled service"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.6, 1.15, 1.46, 2.34, 2.87, 3.12, 3.51, 3.91, 4.06, 4.28]}, {"scene": "o", "kind": "end", "ref": ["status"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 58.87, "t1": 61.4, "shot": "end", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.44, 0.88, 1.06, 1.35, 1.43, 1.53, 1.78, 2.07]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"p": "San Francisco’s original report showed zero co